[align=center]
[size=200][b]Welcome to Switch Vision[/b][/size]
[color=#5B8DEF][i]Live managed-switch visualisation for Home Assistant[/i][/color]
[/align]
[hr]
Switch Vision discovers supported managed switches, creates the required telemetry configuration and displays live switch state on an interactive front-panel dashboard inside Home Assistant.

[notice][b]Current public Core release: v2.6.8[/b]
[b]Protected Gold baseline: v2.5.0 Gold[/b]
Switch Vision components are independently versioned. Use the Switch Vision Installer to see the current version of every installed component.[/notice]

[size=150][b]What Switch Vision includes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Switch Vision Core and interactive switch dashboard
[*]Native Home Assistant Switch Vision sidebar panel
[*]Switch Vision Hub / Discovery
[*]Exact-model device detection and registry
[*]Automatic SNMP2MQTT configuration generation
[*]Optional UniFi Integration API support through UniFi2MQTT
[*]Interactive port, LED, status-panel and faceplate calibration
[*]Calibration Profile management
[*]Maintenance and diagnostics tools
[*]Support My Switch contribution system
[*]Privacy processing and contributor recognition controls
[/list]

[size=150][b]The normal workflow[/b][/size]
[code]Switch Vision Installer
→ Install / Update All
→ Restart Home Assistant Core when requested
→ Open Switch Vision Hub
→ Add your switch
→ Run Discovery
→ Open Switch Vision from the sidebar[/code]

For most users there is no YAML to write manually.

[notice][b]Only one repository normally needs to be added manually:[/b]
https://github.com/zemerdon/switch-vision-installer
The Installer manages the remaining Switch Vision components.[/notice]

[size=150][b]Hardware support[/b][/size]
Switch Vision support is based on evidence from the exact hardware model — not assumptions based on a similar switch.

[code]Detected
→ Experimental
→ Community Validated
→ Confirmed Supported[/code]

